WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.033
-I'm so happy to see you,
Marc Maron.

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.334
-Nice to see you, too, man.

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:04.601
-We got a full audience here.

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:07.033
We're live, in person.
I mean, this is happening.

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:08.801
[ Cheering and applause ]
Marc Maron!

00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:10.400
-The last time,
I was on my porch.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.801
-That's right.
-Just sitting on the porch,

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:13.467
talking to you.
-You were Zooming me

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.534
and I appreciate that
because we needed guests.

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:18.167
-That was the best, man,
just not going anywhere.

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:20.000
[ Laughter ]
-No! This is the best.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.934
-I'm doing "The Tonight Show"
on the porch.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.267
[ Laughter ]
-No! This is the best.

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:24.567
You're doing "The Tonight Show"
-You're right here.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:26.167
-in "The Tonight Show," yeah.
-You're right there!

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:27.434
-Right here!
-Oh, man.

00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:29.934
-You look great!
-I dressed. I got dressed.

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:30.934
[ Laughter ]
I didn't get food on me.

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:32.534
Big day.
-Big day.

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:34.868
[ Laughter ]
You didn't get food.
You do. You look fantastic.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.334
-I'm aging.

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:38.067
I don't know if you can tell,
but I'm --

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:39.667
[ Laughter ]
What are you laughing at?

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:41.934
-No.
-Why are they laughing, Jimmy?

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:44.100
-No one's laughing.
-But it's weird.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.100
I don't know that
I'm getting older

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.801
because, like, okay,
I don't have kids.

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:49.234
And I think, if you have kids,

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:51.467
you can kind of see yourself
dying in your kids, you know?

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:52.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:54.367
Because you're kind of like --

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:55.968
you're kind of like,
"Happy Birthday."

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:57.901
"It's happening.
Oh, my God!"

00:00:57.901 --> 00:01:00.734
[ Laughter ]
Right? Mirrors, you know,

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:01.701
you get used to mirrors.

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:02.934
Like you can just
rationalize it.

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:05.334
You see yourself every day.
You do your poses

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:07.434
[ Laughter ]
and you don't tell.
You can't tell.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.567
But if I see a picture, man,
if I see a picture of me,

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:11.501
it's like, "Oh, my God!

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:13.033
When did my head get old?

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:14.200
I got an old head!"

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.400
[ Laughter ]
-Old head?
-Yeah.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.167
No matter what I do down here,
head's still old.

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:19.601
[ Laughter ]
Head's still old.

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.434
Like people are like,
"Nice jacket.

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:23.300
Old head."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:24.934
-You got an old head.
-I got an old head.

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:26.467
-Aside from getting older,
I mean,

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:28.033
you look good.
I mean, how do you feel?

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:30.767
-I'm alright. You know, I --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:34.000
Well, you know, I believe --
I think I'm wrong,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.834
but I think I hide
my anxiety pretty well.

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:38.601
[ Laughter ]
-I think you do.
-Why are you laughing?

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:39.934
Why are you laughing?
-I'm not, no. I was thinking

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:42.334
about something else.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:44.434
-No, because I have tools.
I'm an anxious person.

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:47.000
I'm anxious.
I get filled with dread a lot,

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.334
but I've got some tools.
I'll share them.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:50.701
Some other people,
maybe they're anxious.

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:52.701
About ten times a day,
I have to say this to myself --

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:54.167
"Dude, you're not in a hurry!

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:55.934
[ Laughter ]
You're not in a hurry!"

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.567
You know what I mean?
Because like

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:59.701
I'll wake up and be like,
"Oh, man, I gotta...!"

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:00.734
And like you have nothing.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:02.267
There's nothing.
You have nothing.

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:04.100
[ Laughter and applause ]
You don't need to finish
the sentence.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.534
"I gotta --"
No, you don't.

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:07.367
-You're coming into the day
a little hot.

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:09.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:11.000
-Yeah. You don't gotta
do anything.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.234
-No, no.
Just make the coffee.

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:14.267
I drink about a quart of coffee

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.200
[ Laughter ]
and then I just kind of like

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.100
caffeinate myself
into sort of an exhaustion.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.734
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my gosh.
But you're back on tour.

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:24.400
Do you like going on tour?
-Well, yeah, I was just in --

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.234
I did Providence and Boston
and I did Tarrytown.

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:30.234
I did Portland, Maine;
Providence.

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:31.868
It's weird going back
to these places where I started

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.868
because my car got stolen

00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:36.701
when I was doing a gig
in Providence in 1989.

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:39.267
[ Laughter ]
-Exactly. You don't forget
those things.

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:41.000
-No, you don't. And I went
to the police station.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.200
They still haven't found it.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:45.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.567
-But it's good that they're
on it, still,

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:48.968
you know what I mean?
-They're still thinking
about it.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.434
[ Laughter ]
-It's not like television.

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:52.167
These things take a while
to solve.

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:54.067
-"We can't help you, Marc."
But this is called

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:55.634
This May Be the Last Time Tour.

00:02:55.634 --> 00:02:56.934
-Yes.
-Why?

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:59.634
-Why not? Does anyone know
what's going to happen?

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:02.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.300
Am I wrong in thinking
that we're in trouble, maybe?

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:09.067
[ Laughter ]
I mean, don't we
all kind of know it?

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:10.734
I don't have any hope.

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:14.334
[ Laughter ]
But --

00:03:14.334 --> 00:03:16.200
I mean, who has hope?
What are you, seven?

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:20.367
-What?!
-Magical thinking.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:23.033
No, what I'm saying --
No, listen to me.

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:25.334
I do believe like
people will adapt. They will.

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:27.400
I think we're maybe
three years away

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.200
from hearing this
on the streets of New York --

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:33.234
"You know, 130's not that hot.

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:35.367
Once you get out in it,
you get used to it.

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:37.801
Just don't stay out there
past the allotted time --

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.767
30 minutes.
Bring a water pack. Be careful."

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:42.667
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God. Hope not.

00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:44.000
-Well, you know,
I don't know what to do.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.667
Do you know what to do?
It seems like out of our control

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:48.200
and like we all know
that the environment is terrible

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.000
and we feel guilty about it,

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.601
but I think in the back
of our heads,

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:53.033
most of us are like,
"Well, you know,

00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:55.367
that Swedish teenager has it
under control," you know?

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:59.200
[ Laughter ]
Like I don't want to --

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.501
-Greta Thunberg?

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:01.501
[ Applause ]
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:05.467
-That's so funny.

00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:07.567
I don't want to get
in the way.

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:10.601
I don't want to get in the way
of whatever Greta's doing.

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:11.901
She's young.
She's focused.

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:13.701
She's going to nail it.

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:15.434
[ Laughter and applause ]
We're going to be okay.

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:16.968
-That's really funny.

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:21.501
You get tickets
at wtfpod.com/tour.
-And get them there.

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:23.467
People just Google
"Mark Marion tickets"

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:25.767
and they're taken
to a scalper site immediately

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:27.467
and then they tweet at me,
go like,

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.267
"Why is it $900?"

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:31.300
[ Laughter ]
I'm like, "Why are you
so stupid?"

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.334
[ Laughter ]
-Alright, don't say that.

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:35.033
Let's talk
about "The Bad Guys."

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:37.934
You're in this new
animated film, "The Bad Guys."

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:39.534
You're the voice of Mr. Snake.

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:41.868
-That's correct.
-Now, what do you do?

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:44.734
What does Marc Maron do to get
into character for it?

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:46.267
-I've done a few
animated characters

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:48.601
and they're just different
degrees of me yelling.

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:51.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.734 --> 00:04:53.400
Like here, I'll do a couple
of my animated voices for you.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:54.834
-Let me close my eyes.
-There's this guy!

00:04:54.834 --> 00:04:56.467
How about this guy?!
-Yeah, I like him.

00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:58.234
-And then, like,
"What are you doing?!"

00:04:58.234 --> 00:04:59.434
[ Laughter ]
There's that guy.

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:00.934
Two totally different
characters.

00:05:00.934 --> 00:05:02.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:04.100
-Wow. Isn't that amazing?
-Thank you.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:05.400
-Right before your eyes.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:09.000
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.601
You are very funny in this

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:11.868
and I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:14.801
Here's Marc Maron as Mr. Snake
in "The Bad Guys."

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:15.834
Take a look at this.

00:05:15.834 --> 00:05:16.801
[ Siren wailing ]
-[ Chuckle ]

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:18.367
-Wolf,

00:05:18.367 --> 00:05:19.534
what are you doing?

00:05:19.534 --> 00:05:21.200
-What?
-Yeah!

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.601
-Oh, that!

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:24.434
I-I-I'm sorry.

00:05:24.434 --> 00:05:25.767
I thought it was, uh, obvious.

00:05:25.767 --> 00:05:27.601
We're going to go good.

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:29.934
[ Siren wailing ]

00:05:29.934 --> 00:05:31.167
-You totally lost me.

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:33.334
-I told him to stop drinking
out of the toilet.

00:05:33.334 --> 00:05:35.033
-Hey, did you get hit
on the head?

00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:37.534
-What? No, I didn't.
-My cousin got hit on the head

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:40.434
with an anchor and, after that,
he only swam in a circle.

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:42.767
-No, no, guys, guys, guys.
You're not following me.

00:05:42.767 --> 00:05:46.100
The bad guys become
the good guys

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:50.100
so we can stay the bad guys,
you know what I mean?

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:53.200
-Bad guys acting good?

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.133
It's the ultimate bad guy thing!

00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:56.501
It's fantastic!

00:05:56.501 --> 00:05:58.167
Wolf, you're a genius!

00:05:58.167 --> 00:05:59.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:01.334
-That's exactly right.
-[ As Mr. Snake ] Fantastic.

00:06:01.334 --> 00:06:02.133
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:03.234
-Are you still --

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:08.300
-What?
-Are you still collecting vinyl?

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.667
Get any new vinyl?
-Yeah, I do. I still do
the vinyl thing.

00:06:10.667 --> 00:06:11.801
I'd like to think that like

00:06:11.801 --> 00:06:13.834
I discovered vinyl
before everybody else.

00:06:13.834 --> 00:06:15.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:16.634
Like I think when I started
buying records,

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:18.567
like two weeks later,
everyone in the world

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:20.200
started buying records.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.701
But here's the weird thing
about buying records, is,

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:26.100
if you go, if you're a guy
who shops at record stores,

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.801
it's usually guys my age,
you know, and,

00:06:28.801 --> 00:06:30.968
[ Laughter ]
you know, you'll be in the
record store for about an hour

00:06:30.968 --> 00:06:33.534
and, within that hour,
someone will walk in

00:06:33.534 --> 00:06:35.367
that looks exactly like you.

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:36.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.868 --> 00:06:38.100
And you just have this moment

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.734
where you both look
at each other and go like,

00:06:39.734 --> 00:06:41.734
"I don't know.
I don't know what's happened."

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:43.901
[ Laughter ]
And then I go, "I know.
it's weird, right?

00:06:43.901 --> 00:06:45.467
But, hey, cool boots.

00:06:45.467 --> 00:06:46.534
Old head."

00:06:46.534 --> 00:06:48.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.634
-Old head.
Marc Maron, everybody!

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:53.033
"The Bad Guys" hits theaters
this Friday.

00:06:53.033 --> 00:06:56.567
Check out wtfpod.com
for information

00:06:56.567 --> 00:06:57.968
on Marc's stand-up tour.
We'll be right back.

